    "blurb": "The band builds momentum toward an electrifying Turn On Your Lovelight, where Jerry delivers a feral solo and Pigpen drives the groove with wild organ. Earlier numbers are steady though some listeners note a slower start. Overall performance is strong with standout vocals from Bob.",
    "review": "On April 11, 1970 at the Fillmore West, the Grateful Dead rolled out a first set that wove together folk‑rock staples and a soaring psychedelic climax. After a measured opening—Cold Rain And Snow, Dire Wolf, and a handful of early‑era tunes—the group surged into a monster Dark Star > Saint Stephen > Not Fade Away sequence before unleashing an unforgettable Turn On Your Lovelight. Reviewers consistently praise Pigpen’s organ frenzy and vocal antics on Lovelight, and Jerry’s “delightfully feral minor mode” solo that rides the song’s high‑energy wave. Bob Weir is noted for building his vocal intensity and guitar work leading into the climax. While a few listeners felt the early portion lacked punch, the show’s centerpiece more than makes up for it, delivering one of the era’s most vivid Lovelight moments captured on an excellent soundboard recording.",
